From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:05:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: AOT_GROUP=N compiles about N lifted functions
 into one object (#18)

Option B of the recompilation cost. Every small object takes a 4 KB block
and repeats its ELF headers and symbols: 622,259 objects held 2.7 GB of
content in 6.3 GB on disk. With AOT_GROUP=N the IR of about N functions is
merged by llvm-link and compiled once, with a .grp beside the object. The
groups are cut by a hash of the addresses, so a change recompiles its group
and not the ones after it. A group that cannot be merged, or where a function
needs a symbol the runtime lacks, is split into one object per function.
Off by default. On 1,000 generated functions with N=64: 26 files against
2,000, 1.4 MB on disk against 8.7 MB, half the CPU. cache-stats counts the
.grp files and the run report has group_hits, group_builds, group_splits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Option B of the recompilation cost: one object for about N functions, opt-in with AOT_GROUP
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#18

